{"name":"Wharf Wind","hex":"#bbbcae","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wharf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artificial landing place for ships on a riverbank or shore.","Any bank of a river or shore of a sea."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To secure by a wharf.","To place on a wharf."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wharf"},{"term":"wind","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Real or perceived movement of atmospheric air usually caused by convection or differences in air pressure.","Air artificially put in motion by any force or action."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To blow air through a wind instrument or horn to make a sound.","To cause (someone) to become breathless, as by a blow to the abdomen, or by physical exertion, running, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wharf","blocks":[{"text":"A wharf, quay, staith, or staithe is a structure on the shore of a harbor or on the bank of a river or canal where ships may dock to load and unload cargo or passengers. Such a structure includes one or more berths, and may also include piers, warehouses, or other facilities necessary for handling the ships. Wharves are often considered to be a series of docks at which boats are stationed. A marginal wharf is connected to the shore along its full length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Houston_Ship_Channel_Barbours_Cut.jpg/330px-Houston_Ship_Channel_Barbours_Cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wharf"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Wharf_Quay.jpg/500px-Wharf_Quay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Wharf_Quay.jpg/1280px-Wharf_Quay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Wharf_Quay.jpg/500px-Wharf_Quay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wharf under construction on the Upper Mississippi in Fountain City, Wisconsin[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWharf_Quay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Rinlo_%28RPS_24-07-2020%29_Muelle%2C_se%C3%B1al_de_tr%C3%A1fico_de_peligro.png/500px-Rinlo_%28RPS_24-07-2020%29_Muelle%2C_se%C3%B1al_de_tr%C3%A1fico_de_peligro.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Rinlo_%28RPS_24-07-2020%29_Muelle%2C_se%C3%B1al_de_tr%C3%A1fico_de_peligro.png/1280px-Rinlo_%28RPS_24-07-2020%29_Muelle%2C_se%C3%B1al_de_tr%C3%A1fico_de_peligro.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Rinlo_%28RPS_24-07-2020%29_Muelle%2C_se%C3%B1al_de_tr%C3%A1fico_de_peligro.png/500px-Rinlo_%28RPS_24-07-2020%29_Muelle%2C_se%C3%B1al_de_tr%C3%A1fico_de_peligro.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traffic sign: Quayside or river bank ahead. Unprotected quayside 